#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Adopt a blank or established repository; `ballast init` runs this file.

Usage: tools/init --project ROOT --ref REF [--description TEXT]
                  [--stack python|node|rust|go|neutral]

Only the global `ballast` command is expected to call it, from the fetched
standard (or BALLAST_STANDARD_DIR), under `python3 -I -S`. One stage sequence
serves every repository: `check`, `inspect` (a fixed, size-bounded list of
evidence files, read as data and never executed), `choose` (a blank
repository's description and stack: a flag, else a terminal prompt, else a
refusal), `plan`, then the first write: `git-init` (only without a
repository), `ignore` (setup's block, appended once), `write` (absent
project-owned files only, created exclusively and never through a link),
`patch` (every change to an existing file goes into the ignored
`.ballast/init/proposed.patch`), `install` (this version's tools/setup),
`verify` and `report`.

Init never runs a command it detects, never records trust, and never commits,
pushes or adds a remote. Exit status: 0 when no readiness check is
`not-ready`; 1 on a failed stage or a `not-ready` check; 2 on a refusal, which
before `git-init` leaves the directory untouched.
"""

